<title>FINLAND: MERITA STAKE IN LASSILA FALLS BELOW 10 PCT.</title>
<headline>MERITA STAKE IN LASSILA FALLS BELOW 10 PCT.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1997-07-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Plastic and cleaning equipment maker Lassila &amp; Tikanoja said on Friday Finnish Merita Oy's banking unit's stake in it had fallen below 10 percent to 6.78 percent.</p>
<p>&quot;Merita Bank's ownership stake is .... 6.78 percent (268,000 shares),&quot; it said.</p>
<p>Lassila stated in its 1996 annual report that Merita was its second largest owner after insurer Pohjola with 10.6 percent of shares and votes on February 14 this year.</p>
<p>Pohjola's stake was 12.9 percent, it said.</p>
<p>-- Helsinki newsroom +358-9-680 50 245, news@reuters.fi</p>
